Being a father is
the best thing in the world.

12:37.239 --> 12:38.404
How old are your kids?

12:38.406 --> 12:39.639
Well, my son is 15

12:39.641 --> 12:42.609
and my secret daughter
is going to be 11 this year.

12:43.744 --> 12:44.978
Your... your
secret daughter?

12:44.980 --> 12:48.248
Yeah, she looks a lot
like my secret wife.

12:53.988 --> 12:56.556
You know, kids are amazing.

12:56.558 --> 12:59.325
You know? You get to pass
all this knowledge down

12:59.327 --> 13:02.161
to this little person
and-and shape their mind.

13:02.163 --> 13:04.063
Like, you know,
how to talk to girls

13:04.065 --> 13:06.633
and how to be there for
your friends when they need you.

13:06.635 --> 13:08.167
Oh, you can teach them
your ability

13:08.169 --> 13:11.337
to always be in the bathroom
whenever the dinner check comes.

13:12.206 --> 13:15.208
That's pure instinct.

13:15.210 --> 13:18.111
Can't be taught.

13:20.181 --> 13:22.849
You know, all my memories
revolve around my dad.

13:22.851 --> 13:26.519
The time he threw my Tamagotchi
down the garbage disposal.

13:26.521 --> 13:29.188
Time he made a pass
at my prom date.

13:29.190 --> 13:32.725
Time he divorced my mom
and married my prom date.

13:35.029 --> 13:36.129
Guys.

13:36.131 --> 13:37.997
Guys, it's
the hospital.

13:37.999 --> 13:39.932
Oh, if it's one of
my patients, I'm not here.

13:40.768 --> 13:41.934
Oh, don't worry.
If I'm your

13:41.936 --> 13:43.236
kid's doctor,
I won't do that.

13:44.071 --> 13:46.272
It's what you say.

13:46.274 --> 13:48.007
Kathy's in labor!

13:48.009 --> 13:49.075
We got to go!

13:49.077 --> 13:50.043
I'll get an Uber.

13:50.045 --> 13:51.177
I'll go grab the car seat.

13:51.179 --> 13:52.345
I'll get the
diaper bag.

13:53.348 --> 13:55.181
Oh, God, that's the pizza guy.

13:55.183 --> 13:56.115
Um... hey, Alan,

13:56.117 --> 13:57.417
could you pay
the pizza guy?

13:57.419 --> 13:59.585
I'm in the bathroom!

13:59.587 --> 14:01.788
How does he do it?

14:04.258 --> 14:06.826
♪ &lt;i>Men.&lt;/i> ♪

14:06.828 --> 14:09.128
Hey, you know,
I-I appreciate you guys coming,

14:09.130 --> 14:10.663
but you really
don't have to stay.

14:10.665 --> 14:12.532
Are you kidding?
We want to be here.

14:12.534 --> 14:13.800
You know what
they say.

14:13.802 --> 14:16.102
"To raise a child, it
takes the Village People."

14:16.104 --> 14:18.271
Hey, guys?

14:18.273 --> 14:20.106
I think I may have
gotten way too high.

14:20.108 --> 14:21.841
Can somebody take me
to the hospital?

14:21.843 --> 14:23.776
You're in a hospital.

14:25.146 --> 14:26.579
Whoa.

14:26.581 --> 14:27.714
How'd you do that?

14:28.649 --> 14:30.650
I wonder why
we haven't heard anything.

14:30.652 --> 14:33.519
They took Kathy to the delivery
room, like, an hour ago.

14:33.521 --> 14:35.888
Sometimes the baby just
doesn't want to come out.

14:35.890 --> 14:37.590
I mean, put yourself
in its position.

14:37.592 --> 14:39.158
For nine months,
you've been floating

14:39.160 --> 14:40.393
in the world's
nicest waterbed.

14:40.395 --> 14:43.396
Then somebody opens a trap door,
all the water flows out,

14:43.398 --> 14:46.332
a set of salad tongs grabs you
by the head and yanks you out,

14:46.334 --> 14:47.967
and then some guy
you never seen before

14:47.969 --> 14:49.836
starts slapping
you on the ass.

14:49.838 --> 14:52.772
Reminds me of a trip
I took to Tijuana once.

14:54.808 --> 14:57.243
Aw, look at how cute
that one is.

14:57.245 --> 14:58.945
Yeah, she's got
a nice rack, too.

14:58.947 --> 15:01.381
What are you looking at?

15:01.383 --> 15:03.983
The hot nurse.
What are you looking at?

15:03.985 --> 15:05.618
That baby.

15:05.620 --> 15:08.421
Ugh! You guys are sick.

15:10.758 --> 15:12.925
So have you guys decided
on a name for the baby yet?

15:12.927 --> 15:14.827
Oh, no, not yet.
No.

15:14.829 --> 15:15.928
It's such a big
responsibility.

15:15.930 --> 15:17.463
I don't want
to give him a name

15:17.465 --> 15:18.831
that other kids
can make fun of.

15:18.833 --> 15:21.100
Well, bad news.
Every name can be made fun of.

15:21.102 --> 15:22.702
That's not true.

15:22.704 --> 15:23.736
Really?

15:23.738 --> 15:25.505
How's your pond, Walden?

15:26.807 --> 15:29.942
It's an intellectual insult,
but it still stings.

15:31.111 --> 15:34.247
I was "Larry the fairy"
all through high school.

15:34.249 --> 15:37.316
Oh, no way!
I was "Barry the fairy."

15:37.318 --> 15:40.186
Somebody noticed
that you could rearrange

15:40.188 --> 15:41.721
the letters of "Alan,"
and I became

15:41.723 --> 15:44.157
"Little Anal Harper."

15:44.159 --> 15:45.224
My name's "Herb."

15:45.226 --> 15:46.592
Kids skipped the clever puns

15:46.594 --> 15:48.761
and just shoved my head
down a toilet.

15:48.763 --> 15:51.130
Well, I'm sure
there are plenty of names

15:51.132 --> 15:52.999
that kids can't
make jokes about.

15:53.001 --> 15:55.468
Mr. and Mr. Harper-Schmidt?

15:55.470 --> 15:56.969
Yeah, nothing to
worry about there.

15:56.971 --> 16:00.206
Just the hyphenated last name
of the two gay dads.

16:00.208 --> 16:01.441
So how's Kathy?

16:01.443 --> 16:02.842
She's doing fine.

16:02.844 --> 16:05.144
So is your brand-new baby boy.

16:05.146 --> 16:07.814
Oh, my God,
we got a boy!

16:07.816 --> 16:10.516
I get a do-over for Jake!

16:10.518 --> 16:13.352
I only have to worry
about one penis!

16:13.354 --> 16:14.921
I like to wear
women's underwear!

16:14.923 --> 16:17.256
What?

16:17.258 --> 16:20.793
I thought we were
confessing things.

16:22.262 --> 16:24.130
There he is.

16:24.132 --> 16:25.865
Aw...

16:27.801 --> 16:30.169
He's got your nose
and Alan's eyes.

16:31.004 --> 16:32.972
Larry, I told you
before that...

16:33.907 --> 16:36.843
Thank you, Larry.

16:36.845 --> 16:39.078
Look at him.
He's so amazing.

16:39.080 --> 16:40.780
I can't think of
anything more beautiful

16:40.782 --> 16:42.315
than what I'm looking
at right now.

16:42.317 --> 16:44.884
Yeah. Mm-hmm.
It's true, that's the truth.

16:44.886 --> 16:47.253
But how much more
beautiful would it be

16:47.255 --> 16:49.522
if those two nurses just
started making out right now?

16:49.524 --> 16:51.991
Mm-hmm.
Oh, yeah.

16:51.993 --> 16:54.293
♪ &lt;i>Men.&lt;/i> ♪

16:56.430 --> 16:57.897
Hey.

16:57.899 --> 16:59.365
How you doing?

16:59.367 --> 17:01.067
I'm good.

17:01.069 --> 17:02.568
Tired.

17:02.570 --> 17:04.103
Sore.

17:04.105 --> 17:06.739
Look at this little guy.

17:06.741 --> 17:08.007
Can I hold him?

17:08.009 --> 17:09.709
Uh, sure.

17:12.513 --> 17:15.314
Oh, he is the cutest thing ever.

17:15.316 --> 17:17.049
Mm-hmm.

17:17.051 --> 17:19.552
Hey, hey... high-five.

17:19.554 --> 17:20.620
You can owe me.

17:21.890 --> 17:24.724
Welcome to the world,
little buddy.

17:24.726 --> 17:26.559
We're gonna have
so much fun.

17:26.561 --> 17:28.494
We're gonna go to
ball games together

17:28.496 --> 17:30.196
and go swimming together

17:30.198 --> 17:33.833
and pick up chick... ens
together.

17:33.835 --> 17:36.168
Smile. Come on.

17:36.170 --> 17:37.937
Okay, uh...

17:37.939 --> 17:40.706
Oh, oh, oh.
Look at that picture.

17:40.708 --> 17:43.543
The two most handsome
men in the world.

17:43.545 --> 17:45.478
And they're both mine.

17:45.480 --> 17:47.146
Oh, oh...

17:47.148 --> 17:48.114
Oh, what's the matter?

17:48.116 --> 17:49.815
Uh, maybe he wants his mommy.

17:49.817 --> 17:51.217
Oh, all right,
come here, little buddy.

17:51.219 --> 17:53.519
Uh, I think he might be hungry.

17:53.521 --> 17:54.854
Oh, of course.

17:54.856 --> 17:56.088
Oh, yeah, of course.

17:56.090 --> 17:57.690
Okay, here.

17:57.692 --> 18:00.059
There.

18:00.061 --> 18:02.862
I miss him already.

18:02.864 --> 18:04.864
Yeah, it's hard to let him go.

18:06.967 --> 18:09.101
Actually, it's impossible.

18:10.504 --> 18:11.871
Oh.

18:11.873 --> 18:13.906
I am so sorry.

18:15.409 --> 18:17.176
Wait. What, uh...
what just happened?

18:17.178 --> 18:19.078
Did I... did I
miss something?

18:21.448 --> 18:23.716
She's keeping the baby.

18:23.718 --> 18:25.585
Uh...

18:25.587 --> 18:27.820
But what-what
about law school?

18:27.822 --> 18:29.488
The-the five-year plan?

18:29.490 --> 18:32.592
After I saw this little guy...

18:32.594 --> 18:34.427
the plan changed.

18:35.929 --> 18:40.533
I mean, before, I couldn't
imagine my life with him.

18:40.535 --> 18:43.269
Now I can't imagine it
without him.

18:43.271 --> 18:46.372
But... but he's gonna
be a great dad.

18:46.374 --> 18:48.307
Alan...
No, no. H-He loves him.

18:48.309 --> 18:50.076
Alan, it's...

18:50.078 --> 18:52.244
Okay, let's-let's just
approach this practically.

18:52.246 --> 18:53.746
Um... how much for the kid?

18:53.748 --> 18:54.981
Uh, I have, uh,

18:54.983 --> 18:56.582
I have $32 on me.

18:56.584 --> 18:58.584
I'm gonna need three dollars
for dinner at ampm,

18:58.586 --> 18:59.685
but the rest is yours.

18:59.687 --> 19:01.587
Believe me, I feel terrible.

19:01.589 --> 19:03.422
You feel terrible?

19:03.424 --> 19:05.992
We're-we're gonna be driving
home with an empty car seat.

19:05.994 --> 19:08.227
And you know what's waiting
for us when we get there?

19:08.229 --> 19:10.463
An empty nursery.
An empty crib.

19:10.465 --> 19:11.931
An empty... uh, uh....

19:11.933 --> 19:13.199
What's that Swedish thing

19:13.201 --> 19:14.867
that, uh, that you
wear like a pouch,

19:14.869 --> 19:17.336
to carry your baby
around like a kangaroo?

19:17.338 --> 19:18.404
Bjorn.

19:18.406 --> 19:19.772
An empty Bjorn!

19:19.774 --> 19:22.341
An empty blue baby Bjorn!

19:22.343 --> 19:24.944
Hard to say,
but even harder to face.

19:24.946 --> 19:27.113
Alan, just... stop.

19:28.215 --> 19:29.682
It's okay.

19:31.118 --> 19:33.452
I wouldn't be able
to give him up either,

19:33.454 --> 19:34.920
so I don't blame you.

19:34.922 --> 19:36.188
Really?

19:36.190 --> 19:38.357
I get it.
You're his mom.

19:38.359 --> 19:40.693
I'm so sorry to put you
through all this.

19:40.695 --> 19:42.194
Don't be sorry.

19:42.196 --> 19:44.797
He's... lucky.

19:44.799 --> 19:47.800
You're both...
very lucky.

19:50.537 --> 19:53.139
This man is a saint.

19:53.141 --> 19:54.340
A damn saint.

19:54.342 --> 19:55.741
Let's go.

19:56.576 --> 19:58.511
Say good-bye, Elliot.

19:58.513 --> 20:00.413
More like "Smelliot."
Alan.

20:00.415 --> 20:02.848
♪ &lt;i>Men.&lt;/i> ♪

20:08.260 --> 20:09.393
♪ &lt;i>Men.&lt;/i> ♪

20:09.395 --> 20:11.495
You doing okay?

20:12.067 --> 20:14.401
Yeah.

20:14.403 --> 20:16.370
Can you show me
the picture of him?

20:16.372 --> 20:18.171
Oh, please, don't put yourself
through this.

20:18.173 --> 20:20.240
Come on, just
one more time.

20:20.242 --> 20:21.642
Okay.

20:21.644 --> 20:23.810
Here.

20:25.980 --> 20:28.615
Look at him.

20:28.617 --> 20:30.350
He's perfect.

20:32.954 --> 20:36.356
I'm sorry this didn't work out
as planned.

20:36.358 --> 20:39.526
He still owes me a high-five.

20:40.428 --> 20:42.029
Don't worry.

20:42.031 --> 20:43.930
We'll find our kid.

20:45.800 --> 20:48.135
I know.

20:48.137 --> 20:51.938
In the meantime,
you're still married to me.

20:54.009 --> 20:56.209
Yes, I am.

20:57.979 --> 21:01.641
Why couldn't Kathy take you
and give me the baby?!

21:03.397 --> 21:09.897
== sync, corrected by &lt;font color=#00FF00>elderman&lt;/font> ==
&lt;font color=#00FFFF>@elder_man&lt;/font>
